# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_audit_r2_regressions.py" "AUDIT R2 REGRESSION GATE: PASS" "audit r2 regression locks" "audit r2 regression locks (three round-2 fixes no other gate covers, each load-bearing): (1) the CROSS-TENANT POISON-PILL is closed — a GitHub login shared across two installations (core.agent's PK is the GLOBAL agent_id) no longer makes the 2nd tenant's seat self-heal try to UPDATE a row behind the 1st tenant's FORCE-RLS wall (Postgres 42501 -> the whole event fails -> GitHub redelivers -> a DETERMINISTIC poison-pill where that tenant's PRs never get a check). The fix [DO NOTHING + a SEPARATE account-scoped UPDATE, in BOTH act_for_claim_with_authority and record_landing_with_authority] is proven STRUCTURALLY (no ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE) AND BEHAVIOURALLY (two real installations, same login, the 2nd does NOT raise and does NOT flip the 1st tenant's agent row); (2) the INCREMENTAL patch path now applies the moat's content-free sanitize to the egress-bound node name + edge dst [it was RAW on a normal push while full ingest sanitized — a steady-state hole]; (3) split-advice no longer SILENTLY over-excludes first-party dirs the extractor admits [a real 'pods/' microservice / 'src/venv/' dir got no advice], while genuine vendored/build dirs [node_modules/ .venv/ dist/] stay excluded" "audit r2 regression locks: cross-tenant poison-pill closed (struct+behavioural over two real installations) + patch-path content-free sanitize + split-advice over-exclusion fixed; content-free throughout" 24
